From 2ce1d48892f3033f15e29c568f395b2f8d912b22 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 21:31:58 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] [FOR-UPSTREAM] ASoC: tas2783-sdw: refuse playback when the
 init writes failed

When the SDCA function initialization writes fail, tas_io_init() leaves
hw_init false, but the firmware download has already set fw_dl_success,
so tas_sdw_hw_params() goes on to play through an amp that is missing
part of its setup. On the ASUS ROG Xbox Ally X20 those writes come from
the ACPI DisCo initialization table and include the posture, which the
BIOS sets differently on each amp.

Refuse playback until the init writes have completed as well, and log
which of the two steps is missing. A stream that is only prepared again
after a resume does not go through hw_params, so check in the port
prepare as well.

Fixes: ca8f3611dcf8 ("ASoC: tas2783A: use acpi initialisation table")
Signed-off-by: Matthew Schwartz <matthew.schwartz@linux.dev>

ally-x20-steamos: backport of Valve linux-integration commit
2ce1d48892f3033f15e29c568f395b2f8d912b22 (mirror
github.com/evlaV/linux-integration, in tag 7.2.10-valve1) to
7.2.7-valve2 (31504582a073), on top of the 0004/0005 backports. On the
X20 the DisCo init writes carry each amp's posture (which side of the
stereo stream it plays); playing without them gives the wrong mix.

Adjusted: tas_port_prep(). 7.2.7-valve2 lacks 5c9979eb1917 ("power
the Function up before preparing the port"), so the tas_dev local
that Valve's hunk relies on is added here, and the new check sits
directly before the port prepare write instead of before the PDE23
power-up block.

Valve-Upstream: 7.2.10-valve1
Derived from: evlaV/linux-integration 2ce1d48892f3 "[FOR-UPSTREAM]
  ASoC: tas2783-sdw: refuse playback when the init writes failed" by
  Matthew Schwartz
---
 sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c | 12 ++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+)

diff --git a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
index e1bdf36f7803..1148eaed555c 100644
--- a/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
+++ b/sound/soc/codecs/tas2783-sdw.c
@@ -1010,6 +1010,11 @@ static s32 tas_sdw_hw_params(struct snd_pcm_substream *substream,
 		return -EINVAL;
 	}
 
+	if (!tas_dev->hw_init) {
+		dev_err(tas_dev->dev, "error playback without init writes");
+		return -EINVAL;
+	}
+
 	sdw_stream = snd_soc_dai_get_dma_data(dai, substream);
 	if (!sdw_stream)
 		return -EINVAL;
@@ -1370,6 +1375,7 @@ static int tas_port_prep(struct sdw_slave *slave, struct sdw_prepare_ch *prep_ch
 			 enum sdw_port_prep_ops pre_ops)
 {
 	struct device *dev = &slave->dev;
+	struct tas2783_prv *tas_dev = dev_get_drvdata(dev);
 	struct sdw_dpn_prop *dpn_prop;
 	u32 addr;
 	int ret;
@@ -1381,6 +1387,12 @@ static int tas_port_prep(struct sdw_slave *slave, struct sdw_prepare_ch *prep_ch
 	addr = SDW_DPN_PREPARECTRL(prep_ch->num);
 	switch (pre_ops) {
 	case SDW_OPS_PORT_PRE_PREP:
+		if (!tas_dev->hw_init) {
+			dev_err(dev, "error port %d prepare without init writes\n",
+				prep_ch->num);
+			return -EINVAL;
+		}
+
 		ret = sdw_write_no_pm(slave, addr, prep_ch->ch_mask);
 		if (ret)
 			dev_err(dev, "prep failed for port %d, err=%d\n",
